---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import Legal from '../components/Legal.astro';
import Tbc from '../components/Tbc.astro';

// DRAFT FOR LEGAL REVIEW. Not legal advice. The medical disclaimer and the
// limitation of liability in particular must be settled by a Malaysian lawyer:
// a clinic cannot contract out of its duty of care, and the wording here is
// written to sit inside that limit rather than to test it.
const title = 'Terms of Service | Cellove Wellness';
const description =
  'The terms on which Cellove Wellness provides this website, including the medical disclaimer and the limits of the information published here.';
---
<Page title={title} description={description}>
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="Terms"
    heading="Terms of Service"
    body="The terms you accept by using this website, and what the information here is and is not."
  />
  <Legal>
    <h2>1. About these terms</h2>
    <p>
      This website is operated by <Tbc what="registered legal name" />, company registration
      number <Tbc what="SSM registration number" />, trading as Cellove Wellness. By using the
      site you accept these terms. If you do not accept them, please do not use the site.
    </p>

    <h2>2. This website is not medical advice</h2>
    <div class="callout">
      <p>
        <strong>Nothing on this website is a diagnosis, a treatment recommendation, or a
        substitute for consulting a doctor.</strong> It is general information about how we
        think and what we consider.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p>
      Reading this site, sending an enquiry or messaging us on WhatsApp does not create a
      doctor-patient relationship. That begins only at a consultation, after a doctor has
      taken a history and examined you.
    </p>
    <p>
      Whether any approach is appropriate for you is decided in consultation and cannot be
      decided from a web page. Do not delay seeking medical attention, or stop treatment a
      doctor has prescribed, because of something you read here.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>If you are having a medical emergency, call 999 or go to the nearest emergency
      department.</strong> We do not monitor this website, email or WhatsApp outside working
      hours, and neither is a route for urgent care.
    </p>

    <h2>3. No promises about outcomes</h2>
    <p>
      We make no claim and give no guarantee that any approach will produce any particular
      result. Individual responses differ, and suitability is assessed case by case.
    </p>
    <p>
      Health advertising in Malaysia is regulated by the Medicine (Advertisement and Sale)
      Act 1956 and the requirements of the Medical Advertisements Board. The content of this
      site is written to stay inside those limits. If you believe something here overstates
      what we can do, tell us at <Tbc what="general enquiries email" /> and we will review it.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Enquiries are not bookings</h2>
    <p>
      Sending the enquiry form or a WhatsApp message asks us to get in touch. It does not
      reserve an appointment and does not commit either of us to anything. An appointment
      exists only once we have confirmed it with you directly.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may decline an enquiry, and we will say so plainly where what you are asking about
      is not something we should be handling.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Using the site</h2>
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>use the site unlawfully, or to attempt to gain access to parts of it that are not public;</li>
      <li>interfere with its operation, or submit anything designed to damage it;</li>
      <li>submit false information, or someone else&rsquo;s personal data without their permission;</li>
      <li>copy substantial parts of the site for commercial use without our written permission.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Our content</h2>
    <p>
      The text, diagrams, photographs, logo and design of this site belong to us or to our
      licensors and are protected by copyright. You may read, print and share pages for your
      own personal, non-commercial use, keeping any attribution intact.
    </p>
    <p>
      The two explanatory figures on this site describe general principles of evidence
      appraisal and delivery. They carry no measurements and are not data about our own
      results. They may be quoted for educational purposes with attribution.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Other people&rsquo;s sites</h2>
    <p>
      We link to WhatsApp and to social media platforms. Those are run by other companies
      under their own terms and privacy policies, and we are not responsible for them. A link
      is not an endorsement.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Availability</h2>
    <p>
      We try to keep the site available and accurate, but we do not promise it will be
      uninterrupted or error-free. We may change, suspend or withdraw any part of it without
      notice. Information may become out of date between reviews.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent Malaysian law allows, we are not liable for loss arising from reliance on
      general information published on this website, from the site being unavailable, or from
      your use of any third-party site we link to.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Nothing in these terms limits or excludes our liability for death or personal
      injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or for anything else that cannot lawfully be
      excluded.</strong> In particular, these terms do not affect the duty of care owed to you
      as a patient once you are under our clinical care.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of Malaysia, and the courts of Malaysia have
      exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute arising from them.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms. The date at the top shows when they last changed, and the
      version published here is the one that applies.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <Tbc what="registered legal name" />, <Tbc what="registered address" />,
      <Tbc what="general enquiries email" />, <Tbc what="business phone" />.
    </p>
  </Legal>
</Page>
